    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0254" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">314.115C43/103: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-09T15:00:00-04:00">May 9, 1929—3
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Voluminous evidence has been submitted by P. W. Shufeldt in support of
                    request that Department of State espouse his claim <pb facs="0255" n="137"
                        xml:id="pg137"/> against Government of Guatemala on account of attempted
                    cancelation of contract.</p>
                <p>The Department is studying the case and, as at present advised, considers it
                    probable that it will be under duty of presenting claim.</p>
                <p>You may bring the foregoing to the attention of the appropriate authorities
                    since, confidentially, this is considered advisable in view of the apparent
                    intention of the Government of Guatemala to grant promptly to another person
                    contract covering Shufeldt’s territory.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
